---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms"
  description="Terms of use for Image Identifier — informational evidence only, not certification."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-fg m-0">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted leading-relaxed">
      By using Image Identifier, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use the tool.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-fg mt-10 mb-3">Informational tool only</h2>
    <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">
      Results describe evidence available in a file you select. They are not a certificate of
      authenticity, legal opinion, journalistic verification, or forensic expert report. Do not rely
      on this tool as the sole basis for consequential decisions.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-fg mt-10 mb-3">Your responsibility</h2>
    <ul class="text-muted pl-5 leading-relaxed space-y-2">
      <li>Only analyze files you have the right to inspect.</li>
      <li>Understand that missing signals do not prove authenticity.</li>
      <li>Understand that present signals can be incomplete, altered, or conflicting.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-fg mt-10 mb-3">Availability</h2>
    <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">
      The service is provided “as is.” Features may change, fail on some devices, or be unavailable
      (including optional checks that require a model download).
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-fg mt-10 mb-3">Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, operators of Image Identifier are not liable for damages
      arising from use of the tool or reliance on its results.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-muted">
      <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
      <span class="mx-2">·</span>
      <a href="/">Back to the tool</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
